==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Unclear, though it was coined in the 19th century. Possibilities include:
* ''[[kanata]]'' meaning "village" in Saint-Lawrence Iroquoian
* ''Can''ada + ''[[-uc]]'' ([[Algonquian]] noun suffix)
* ''[[Connaught]]'', an obscure term for [[Ireland|Irish]]-French-Canadians.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kəˈnʌk/}}
* {{hyphenation|Can|uck}}
* {{audio|En-ca-canuck.ogg|Audio (CA)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|occasionally construed as derogatory}} A person of [[Canadian]] citizenship or ancestry.
#: ''I am a sixth generation '''Canuck''', and proud of it.''
# {{sports}} A member of the [[Vancouver]] Canucks professional [[NHL]] [[ice hockey]] team.
# The name of the [[w:Avro Canada CF-100|Avro Canada CF-100]] fighter-bomber

